-(** [make_address info port] returns an address for ZeroMQ communication. *)
+(** [make_address info port] returns an address for ZeroMQ communication.
+
+    Jupyter's connection file separates endpoint from port with ':' only when
+    the transport is tcp. Every other transport carries a filesystem prefix in
+    [ip] rather than an address, and the reference client appends "-<port>" to
+    it. From jupyter_client's [ConnectionFileMixin._make_url]:
+
+    {v
+      if transport == 'tcp':
+          return "tcp://%s:%i" % (ip, port)
+      else:
+          return "%s://%s-%s" % (transport, ip, port)
+    v}
+
+    Upstream formats ["%s://%s:%d"] for every transport, so under
+    [transport: "ipc"] it binds its unix sockets at ["<ip>:<port>"] while every
+    conforming client connects to ["<ip>-<port>"]. Nothing ever meets. *)
 let make_address info port =
-  Format.sprintf "%s://%s:%d" info.transport info.ip port
+  if info.transport = "tcp"
+  then Format.sprintf "tcp://%s:%d" info.ip port
+  else Format.sprintf "%s://%s-%d" info.transport info.ip port
